(function(E){ const x = E["exam-09"] = E["exam-09"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x09-l3"] = {"id":"x09-l3","patterns":["L3-science","PARA-opinion","TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: a project on food waste","tr":"Listening Part 3: gıda israfı üzerine bir proje","fa":"Listening Part 3: پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی دورریز غذا"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow two students discussing a project: choose the two ideas they really mean, and match six schemes to the opinion the students give about each.","tr":"Bu derste bir projeyi tartışan iki öğrenciyi takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: gerçekten kastettikleri iki fikri seçecek ve altı girişimi öğrencilerin her biri hakkında söylediği görüşle eşleştireceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری حرف‌های دو دانشجو را که درباره‌ی یک پروژه بحث می‌کنند دنبال کنی: دو ایده‌ای را که واقعاً منظورشان است انتخاب کنی و شش طرح را با نظری که درباره‌ی هرکدام می‌دهند جور کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: a project on food waste","tr":"Listening Part 3: gıda israfı üzerine bir proje","fa":"Listening Part 3: پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی دورریز غذا"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow two students discussing a project: choose the two ideas they really mean, and match six schemes to the opinion the students give about each.","tr":"Bu derste bir projeyi tartışan iki öğrenciyi takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: gerçekten kastettikleri iki fikri seçecek ve altı girişimi öğrencilerin her biri hakkında söylediği görüşle eşleştireceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری حرف‌های دو دانشجو را که درباره‌ی یک پروژه بحث می‌کنند دنبال کنی: دو ایده‌ای را که واقعاً منظورشان است انتخاب کنی و شش طرح را با نظری که درباره‌ی هرکدام می‌دهند جور کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Options in the box","tr":"Kutudaki seçenek","fa":"گزینه‌های کادر"},"value":"A-H"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: food waste","tr":"Bu sınav: gıda israfı","fa":"این آزمون: دورریز غذا"},"intro":{"en":"Part 3 is a discussion between students. Science, food and health projects are one of the two largest topic groups. The students rarely state an opinion directly: they admit something, then turn with \"but\" or \"what they really...\".","tr":"Part 3 öğrenciler arasındaki bir tartışmadır. Bilim, gıda ve sağlık projeleri en büyük iki konu grubundan biridir. Öğrenciler görüşlerini nadiren doğrudan söyler: bir şeyi kabul eder, sonra \"but\" ya da \"what they really...\" ile yön değiştirirler.","fa":"Part 3 بحثی بین دانشجوهاست. پروژه‌های علم، غذا و سلامت یکی از دو گروه بزرگ موضوع‌اند. دانشجوها کمتر نظرشان را مستقیم می‌گویند: چیزی را قبول می‌کنند و بعد با «but» یا «what they really...» مسیر را عوض می‌کنند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x09-l3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L3-science","PARA-opinion"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Two students prepare a project on food","tr":"İki öğrenci yemek üzerine bir proje hazırlıyor","fa":"دو دانشجو پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی غذا آماده می‌کنند"},"asks":{"en":"Two students react to a report, decide what to put in a presentation, and then give one opinion on each of six local schemes. In the box task, each scheme matches one opinion, and two opinions are never used.","tr":"İki öğrenci bir rapora tepki veriyor, bir sunuma ne koyacaklarına karar veriyor ve sonra altı yerel girişimin her biri hakkında bir görüş bildiriyor. Kutulu görevde her girişim bir görüşle eşleşir; iki görüş hiç kullanılmaz.","fa":"دو دانشجو به یک گزارش واکنش نشان می‌دهند، تصمیم می‌گیرند در ارائه چه بیاورند و بعد درباره‌ی هرکدام از شش طرح محلی یک نظر می‌دهند. در تمرین کادر، هر طرح با یک نظر جور می‌شود و دو نظر هرگز استفاده نمی‌شوند."},"fields":["What surprised them","What to include","Six schemes and one opinion on each"],"words":[{"a":"surprised","b":"I had no idea / that amazed me","tr":"şaşırmış","fa":"متعجب"},{"a":"not new","b":"it’s been in the news for years","tr":"yeni değil","fa":"تازه نیست"},{"a":"too few replies","b":"six answers out of two hundred","tr":"çok az cevap","fa":"جواب‌های خیلی کم"},{"a":"include","b":"show / add / finish on","tr":"dahil etmek","fa":"گنجاندن"},{"a":"depends on","b":"relies on / needs","tr":"... bağlı","fa":"وابسته به"},{"a":"volunteers","b":"helpers / people giving their time","tr":"gönüllüler","fa":"داوطلب‌ها"},{"a":"few people know about it","b":"it’s not well known / nobody mentions it","tr":"az kişi biliyor","fa":"کمتر کسی خبر دارد"},{"a":"difficult to measure","b":"hard to know whether it makes a difference","tr":"ölçmesi zor","fa":"سخت سنجیده می‌شود"},{"a":"brings in money","b":"is financial / they make money","tr":"para kazandırır","fa":"پول درمی‌آورد"},{"a":"in the long term","b":"as adults / for life","tr":"uzun vadede","fa":"در درازمدت"},{"a":"in the countryside","b":"in a village / far from the centre","tr":"kırsalda","fa":"در روستا"},{"a":"cheap to run","b":"doesn’t cost much","tr":"işletmesi ucuz","fa":"ارزان اداره می‌شود"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"People assume X, but...\" The assumption matches one box option; it is the distractor.","tr":"\"İnsanlar X sanıyor ama...\" Bu varsayım kutudaki bir seçenekle eşleşir; çeldirici odur.","fa":"«مردم خیال می‌کنند X، اما...». این تصور با یکی از گزینه‌های کادر جور است؛ همان گزینه‌ی انحرافی است."},{"en":"An idea is suggested and then dropped for a practical reason (no permission, no time). Do not choose it.","tr":"Bir fikir önerilir ve pratik bir nedenle bırakılır (izin yok, vakit yok). Onu seçme.","fa":"ایده‌ای پیشنهاد و بعد به دلیلی عملی کنار گذاشته می‌شود (اجازه نیست، وقت نیست). انتخابش نکن."},{"en":"For \"surprised\", things the speakers \"knew\" or found \"not surprising\" are wrong options.","tr":"\"Şaşırdı\" sorusunda konuşanların \"bildiği\" ya da \"şaşırtıcı bulmadığı\" şeyler yanlış seçeneklerdir.","fa":"برای «تعجب کرد»، چیزهایی که گوینده‌ها «می‌دانستند» یا «عجیب نبود» گزینه‌های غلط‌اند."}],"example":{"lines":[["Student","People think the bus scheme is too expensive, but the council pays for most of it. What worries me is that it only runs twice a day."]],"item":"What does the student say about the bus scheme? A It costs too much.  B The service is not frequent enough.","answer":"B","why":{"en":"\"People think\" gives the distractor (cost). \"Only twice a day\" = not frequent enough.","tr":"\"People think\" çeldiriciyi (maliyet) veriyor. \"Günde sadece iki kez\" = yeterince sık değil.","fa":"«مردم فکر می‌کنند» گزینه‌ی انحرافی (هزینه) را می‌آورد. «فقط دو بار در روز» یعنی به اندازه‌ی کافی مرتب نیست."}}},{"id":"L3-food","ctx":["L3-food","L3-science"],"title":{"en":"Food, health and the mind","tr":"Beslenme, sağlık ve zihin","fa":"غذا، سلامت و ذهن"},"asks":{"en":"Two students, sometimes with a tutor, plan or review a project on food, diet, sleep or how people think and feel. Questions ask what they decide, what they think of a source or a method, what went wrong and what they will do next.","tr":"İki öğrenci, bazen bir hocayla, yiyecek, beslenme, uyku ya da insanların nasıl düşünüp hissettiği üzerine bir projeyi planlar ya da değerlendirir. Sorular neye karar verdiklerini, bir kaynak ya da yöntem hakkında ne düşündüklerini, neyin ters gittiğini ve sırada ne yapacaklarını sorar.","fa":"دو دانشجو، گاهی با یک استاد، پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی غذا، رژیم غذایی، خواب یا اینکه آدم‌ها چطور فکر می‌کنند و چه حسی دارند را برنامه‌ریزی یا بررسی می‌کنند. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند به چه تصمیمی می‌رسند، درباره‌ی یک منبع یا روش چه فکر می‌کنند، چه چیزی خراب شد و قدم بعدی‌شان چیست."},"fields":["What did the survey show about eating habits?","What is the students’ opinion of the article?","Which TWO factors are linked to poor sleep?","What does each study suggest?"],"words":[{"a":"diet","b":"what people eat","tr":"beslenme","fa":"رژیم غذایی"},{"a":"nutrition","b":"the goodness in food","tr":"besin değeri","fa":"تغذیه"},{"a":"ingredients","b":"what it's made from","tr":"içindekiler","fa":"مواد تشکیل‌دهنده"},{"a":"label","b":"the information on the packet","tr":"etiket","fa":"برچسب"},{"a":"obesity","b":"being seriously overweight","tr":"obezite","fa":"چاقی"},{"a":"consumers","b":"the people who buy it","tr":"tüketiciler","fa":"مصرف‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"participants","b":"the people in the study","tr":"katılımcılar","fa":"شرکت‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"linked to","b":"is connected with","tr":"... ile bağlantılı","fa":"مرتبط با"},{"a":"anxiety","b":"worry / feeling stressed","tr":"kaygı","fa":"اضطراب"},{"a":"lifestyle","b":"the way people live","tr":"yaşam tarzı","fa":"سبک زندگی"},{"a":"evidence","b":"data that shows it","tr":"kanıt","fa":"شواهد"},{"a":"misleading","b":"gives the wrong idea","tr":"yanıltıcı","fa":"گمراه‌کننده"},{"a":"sample size","b":"how many people were tested","tr":"örneklem büyüklüğü","fa":"حجم نمونه"}],"traps":[{"en":"The study’s claim and the students’ view are different: \"the article says sugar is the main cause, but I think that’s too simple\".","tr":"Çalışmanın iddiası ile öğrencilerin görüşü farklıdır: \"makale asıl nedenin şeker olduğunu söylüyor ama bence bu fazla basit\".","fa":"ادعای پژوهش با نظر دانشجوها فرق دارد: «مقاله می‌گوید علت اصلی شکر است، ولی به نظرم این خیلی ساده‌انگارانه است»."},{"en":"Survey numbers: \"most people\", \"a few people\" and \"nobody\" lead to different answers.","tr":"Anket sayıları: \"çoğu insan\", \"birkaç kişi\" ve \"hiç kimse\" farklı cevaplara götürür.","fa":"عددهای نظرسنجی: «بیشتر آدم‌ها»، «چند نفر» و «هیچ‌کس» به جواب‌های متفاوت می‌رسند."}],"example":{"lines":[["Student A","The article blames phones for poor sleep."],["Student B","Partly, but the study we read found that late coffee was a bigger factor."],["Student A","True. The data on caffeine was much stronger."]],"item":"What do the students agree is the main factor?  A mobile phones   B late caffeine   C noise","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Phones are only \"partly\" to blame. Both students accept that the caffeine data was stronger.","tr":"Telefonlar yalnızca \"kısmen\" suçlu. İki öğrenci de kafein verisinin daha güçlü olduğunu kabul ediyor.","fa":"گوشی فقط «تا حدی» مقصر است. هر دو دانشجو قبول می‌کنند که داده‌های کافئین قوی‌تر بود."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L3-science"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Two pairs, then a box of eight","tr":"İki çift, sonra sekizli bir kutu","fa":"دو جفت سؤال، بعد یک کادر هشت‌تایی"},"body":{"en":"Questions 21-22 and 23-24: choose TWO letters, A-E. Questions 25-30: match six schemes to eight opinions, A-H, using each letter once. The discussion follows the order of the questions.","tr":"Soru 21-22 ve 23-24: A-E arasından İKİ harf seç. Soru 25-30: altı girişimi sekiz görüşle (A-H) eşleştir, her harfi bir kez kullan. Tartışma soruların sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۱-۲۲ و ۲۳-۲۴: دو حرف از A تا E انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۲۵ تا ۳۰: شش طرح را با هشت نظر (A تا H) جور کن و هر حرف را یک بار به کار ببر. بحث به ترتیب سؤال‌ها جلو می‌رود."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Before you listen, say each box opinion in simpler words: \"depends on people giving their time\" = needs volunteers.","tr":"Dinlemeden önce kutudaki her görüşü daha basit kelimelerle söyle: \"depends on people giving their time\" = gönüllü ister.","fa":"قبل از گوش دادن، هر نظرِ کادر را ساده‌تر بگو: «depends on people giving their time» یعنی داوطلب لازم دارد."},{"en":"Listen for each scheme’s name: it tells you a new question has started.","tr":"Her girişimin adını dinle: yeni bir sorunun başladığını söyler.","fa":"منتظر اسم هر طرح باش: می‌گوید سؤال تازه‌ای شروع شده."},{"en":"Expect two ideas per scheme: one is admitted or ruled out, the other is the opinion.","tr":"Her girişim için iki fikir bekle: biri kabul edilir ya da elenir, diğeri asıl görüştür.","fa":"برای هر طرح دو ایده انتظار داشته باش: یکی پذیرفته یا رد می‌شود و دیگری نظر اصلی است."},{"en":"Cross out each letter once you use it; two letters will be left.","tr":"Kullandığın her harfin üstünü çiz; iki harf artacak.","fa":"هر حرف را که به کار بردی خط بزن؛ دو حرف باقی می‌ماند."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The first idea is often the wrong one","tr":"İlk fikir çoğu zaman yanlış olandır","fa":"ایده‌ی اول اغلب غلط است"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["You hear","It means"],"tr":["Duyduğun","Anlamı"],"fa":["می‌شنوی","یعنی"]},"rows":[["People assume X, but...","X is not their opinion"],["I thought it was X, but...","X is ruled out"],["What they really rely on is...","the answer follows"],["Some people say..., but I think...","the student’s view comes second"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One box answer, step by step","tr":"Bir kutu cevabı, adım adım","fa":"یک جواب کادر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"What do the students say about the cycle scheme? Choose from the box.","item":"Box: A It is popular with older people.  B It needs better advertising.  C It has saved the town money.","lines":[["Student","You’d think older people would avoid it, but plenty use it. My worry is that most students have never even heard of it."]],"answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"A is mentioned, but \"you’d think\" introduces an assumption.","tr":"A’dan söz ediliyor ama \"you’d think\" bir varsayım getiriyor.","fa":"از A حرف زده می‌شود، اما «you’d think» یک تصور را معرفی می‌کند."},{"en":"\"My worry is\" signals the student’s real opinion.","tr":"\"My worry is\", öğrencinin asıl görüşünü gösteriyor.","fa":"«My worry is» نظر واقعی دانشجو را نشان می‌دهد."},{"en":"\"Never even heard of it\" = it needs better advertising: B.","tr":"\"Adını bile duymamışlar\" = daha iyi tanıtım gerekiyor: B.","fa":"«حتی اسمش را نشنیده‌اند» یعنی تبلیغ بهتری لازم دارد: B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"I thought the market would struggle in winter, but it’s been busier than ever. The real problem is finding enough stallholders.\" What is the student’s concern?","options":["getting enough people to run stalls","winter trade","too many customers"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Winter is ruled out (\"busier than ever\"); \"the real problem\" brings the concern.","tr":"Kış eleniyor (\"hiç olmadığı kadar kalabalık\"); \"the real problem\" asıl kaygıyı getiriyor.","fa":"زمستان رد می‌شود («شلوغ‌تر از همیشه»)؛ «the real problem» نگرانی اصلی را می‌آورد."}},"remember":{"en":"Rewrite the box in simple words, wait for the turn, and use each letter only once.","tr":"Kutuyu basit kelimelerle yeniden yaz, dönüşü bekle ve her harfi yalnızca bir kez kullan.","fa":"کادر را با کلمه‌های ساده بازنویسی کن، منتظر نقطه‌ی چرخش بمان و هر حرف را فقط یک بار به کار ببر."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x09-l3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-l3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 3","title":{"en":"A project on food waste","tr":"Gıda israfı üzerine bir proje","fa":"پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی دورریز غذا"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L3-science"],"script":[{"who":"Amira","line":"OK, Ruben, shall we start with the reading? What did you make of the report on household waste?"},{"who":"Ruben","line":"Well, I knew most food is wasted at home rather than in shops or restaurants. That's been in the news for years. But I had no idea bread was the single item people throw away most. I'd have guessed fruit."},{"who":"Amira","line":"Me too. And the other thing that amazed me was the figure for families. I assumed homes with young children would waste the most, but per person they actually waste less than people living alone."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"Because parents plan meals more carefully, I suppose. What I'd expected to see, and didn't, was anything about weekends. The report doesn't break it down by day at all."},{"who":"Amira","line":"No. And it says people underestimate their own waste, which isn't surprising, really. Nobody likes to admit it."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"True. So, for our presentation, what do we actually want to show? I was thinking we could survey the student kitchens in our hall of residence."},{"who":"Amira","line":"I tried something like that last term for another module, and I got six replies out of two hundred. I don't think it's worth it."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"Fair enough. What about photos of the bins behind the supermarket? That would be quite striking."},{"who":"Amira","line":"We'd need the store's permission, and I can't imagine they'd give it. But I like the idea of doing something practical. What if we cooked one dish from leftovers in front of the group?"},{"who":"Ruben","line":"A live demonstration? That would definitely keep people awake. And we could add the food diaries we kept for a week. They show exactly what we threw away."},{"who":"Amira","line":"Yes, the diaries are perfect, they're real data. I'd thought about interviewing a farmer as well, but there just isn't time before the deadline."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"Agreed. So, the cooking demonstration and the diaries. We've got twenty minutes in total, so the cooking will have to be something quick, like a soup or fried rice."},{"who":"Amira","line":"Right. Now the second part: we have to comment on six local schemes. Let's start with the council's leftovers campaign, the posters and leaflets."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"I think it's a good idea in principle, and it doesn't cost much. The problem is that hardly anyone has heard of it. I only found the leaflet because I went looking for it."},{"who":"Amira","line":"Same here. Then there are the community fridges, where shops and neighbours leave food that anyone can take."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"People assume they cost a lot to run, but the electricity is cheap. What they really rely on is the people who check the dates and clean them every day. If those helpers stop coming, the fridge has to close."},{"who":"Amira","line":"And the apps that let cafés sell their surplus food cheaply at the end of the day?"},{"who":"Ruben","line":"They're great if you live in the centre of a big city, where there are dozens of cafés on the app. My parents live in a village, and when they tried it, there was nothing within ten miles."},{"who":"Amira","line":"OK. What about the restaurants that now offer smaller portions?"},{"who":"Ruben","line":"I like them, and some customers say they waste less. But it's very hard to know whether it makes any real difference, because nobody weighs what's left on the plates. A restaurant might say its waste has fallen, but it could just be that fewer customers came in that month."},{"who":"Amira","line":"That's a fair point. And the boxes of misshapen vegetables that farms sell direct to customers?"},{"who":"Ruben","line":"I thought those were mainly about helping the environment, but the farmer I read about said the main benefit is financial. Before, he had to pay to get rid of the odd-shaped carrots. Now he sells them, so he's actually making money from food he used to throw away."},{"who":"Amira","line":"And finally, the compost schemes in primary schools."},{"who":"Ruben","line":"Some people say they're too small to matter, and in terms of tonnes that's probably true. But I think they could have the biggest effect of all. Children who learn to sort their food waste at seven usually keep doing it as adults."},{"who":"Amira","line":"I agree. That's a good point to finish the presentation on."}],"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 21-22. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":21,"n2":22,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO findings in the report surprised the students?","options":["A Most food is wasted at home rather than in shops.","B Bread is the food that is thrown away most often.","C Families with children waste less per person than people living alone.","D People think they waste less than they really do.","E Most food is wasted at weekends."],"correct":[1,2],"evidence":"But I had no idea bread was the single item people throw away most","trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"],"why":{"en":"B \"I had no idea\" and C \"the other thing that amazed me\". A has \"been in the news for years\", D \"isn’t surprising\", and the report says nothing about weekends.","tr":"B \"hiç bilmiyordum\" ve C \"beni şaşırtan diğer şey\". A \"yıllardır haberlerde\", D \"şaşırtıcı değil\", rapor hafta sonlarından hiç söz etmiyor.","fa":"B «اصلاً نمی‌دانستم» و C «چیز دیگری که متعجبم کرد». A «سال‌هاست در خبرهاست»، D «عجیب نیست» و گزارش اصلاً از آخر هفته حرفی نمی‌زند."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 23-24. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":23,"n2":24,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO things will the students include in their presentation?","options":["A results of a survey of student kitchens","B a dish cooked from leftovers","C photographs of supermarket bins","D the food diaries they kept","E an interview with a farmer"],"correct":[1,3],"evidence":"So, the cooking demonstration and the diaries","trap":["TR-ruledout"],"why":{"en":"Ruben sums up: \"the cooking demonstration and the diaries\". The survey got too few replies, the supermarket would not agree, and there is no time for a farmer.","tr":"Ruben özetliyor: \"yemek gösterisi ve günlükler\". Ankete çok az cevap geldi, süpermarket izin vermez, çiftçi için de vakit yok.","fa":"روبن جمع‌بندی می‌کند: «آشپزی جلوی جمع و دفترچه‌ها». نظرسنجی جواب خیلی کمی گرفت، سوپرمارکت اجازه نمی‌دهد و برای کشاورز هم وقت نیست."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 25-30. What do the students say about each of the following food-waste schemes? Choose SIX answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-H, next to Questions 25-30.","qtype":"matching","bank":["A It depends on people giving their time.","B It is too expensive for small businesses.","C It could easily be copied in other towns.","D Few people know about it.","E It works better in cities than in the countryside.","F It may change habits for life.","G It brings in money for the people who run it.","H Its effect is difficult to measure."],"questions":[{"n":25,"kind":"match","prompt":"the council’s leftovers campaign","correct":3,"evidence":"hardly anyone has heard of it","why":{"en":"\"It doesn’t cost much\" rules out B. \"Hardly anyone has heard of it\" = few people know about it.","tr":"\"Pahalı değil\" B’yi eler. \"Neredeyse kimse duymamış\" = az kişi biliyor.","fa":"«هزینه‌ی زیادی ندارد» B را رد می‌کند. «تقریباً هیچ‌کس اسمش را نشنیده» یعنی کم کسی از آن خبر دارد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-ruledout"]},{"n":26,"kind":"match","prompt":"community fridges","correct":0,"evidence":"What they really rely on is the people who check the dates","why":{"en":"People assume they are costly, but the electricity is cheap. They rely on helpers = people giving their time.","tr":"İnsanlar pahalı sanıyor ama elektrik ucuz. Gönüllülere dayanıyor = zamanını veren insanlar.","fa":"مردم خیال می‌کنند پرهزینه است، اما برق ارزان است. به داوطلب‌ها متکی است یعنی آدم‌هایی که وقتشان را می‌گذارند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":27,"kind":"match","prompt":"surplus-food apps","correct":4,"evidence":"if you live in the centre of a big city","why":{"en":"Great in a big city; in his parents’ village \"there was nothing within ten miles\".","tr":"Büyük bir şehirde harika; ailesinin köyünde \"on mil içinde hiçbir şey yoktu\".","fa":"در شهر بزرگ عالی است؛ در روستای پدر و مادرش «تا ده مایل هیچ چیزی نبود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"smaller portions in restaurants","correct":7,"evidence":"it's very hard to know whether it makes any real difference","why":{"en":"\"Very hard to know whether it makes any real difference\" = difficult to measure.","tr":"\"Gerçekten fark yaratıp yaratmadığını bilmek çok zor\" = ölçmesi zor.","fa":"«خیلی سخت است بفهمی واقعاً فرقی می‌کند یا نه» یعنی سنجیدنش سخت است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"boxes of misshapen vegetables","correct":6,"evidence":"so he's actually making money from food he used to throw away","why":{"en":"He thought it was about the environment, but \"the main benefit is financial\": the farmer makes money.","tr":"Çevreyle ilgili sanıyordu ama \"asıl fayda maddi\": çiftçi para kazanıyor.","fa":"فکر می‌کرد بیشتر به محیط زیست مربوط است، اما «فایده‌ی اصلی مالی است»: کشاورز پول درمی‌آورد."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"school compost schemes","correct":5,"evidence":"usually keep doing it as adults","why":{"en":"\"Too small to matter\" is what some people say. Children \"keep doing it as adults\" = it may change habits for life.","tr":"\"Önemsenmeyecek kadar küçük\" bazılarının görüşü. Çocuklar \"yetişkinken de yapmaya devam ediyor\" = alışkanlıkları ömür boyu değiştirebilir.","fa":"«آن‌قدر کوچک که مهم نیست» حرف بعضی‌هاست. بچه‌ها «در بزرگسالی هم ادامه می‌دهند» یعنی ممکن است عادت‌ها را برای همیشه عوض کند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Ruben":{"accent":"North American","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"am_adam"},"role":"Student"},"Amira":{"accent":"British (Southern English)","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"piper","voice":"en_GB-jenny_dioco-medium"},"role":"Student"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 3. You will hear two students, Ruben and Amira, discussing a presentation on food waste. First, you have some time to look at Questions 21 to 24."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 21-24"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 21 to 24."},{"type":"sfx","note":"student kitchen: a kettle in the background at the start, then quiet"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":11},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at Questions 25 to 30."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 25-30"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 25 to 30."},{"type":"lines","from":12,"to":24},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 3. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x09-l3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-l3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Misshapen vegetables\" are vegetables that...","options":["have gone bad","are very small","have an unusual shape"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Misshapen = not the usual shape; they are still good to eat.","tr":"Misshapen = alışılmış biçimde olmayan; yine de yenebilir.","fa":"misshapen یعنی شکلش معمولی نیست؛ هنوز خوردنی است."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"Box: \"Few people know about it.\" Which sentence in a recording matches it?","options":["Hardly anyone can afford it.","Hardly anyone has heard of it.","Hardly anyone likes it."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Hardly anyone has heard of it\" = few people know about it.","tr":"\"Neredeyse kimse duymamış\" = az kişi biliyor.","fa":"«تقریباً هیچ‌کس اسمش را نشنیده» یعنی کم کسی از آن خبر دارد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"People assume the scheme is expensive, but what really matters is that it needs a lot of space.\" Which opinion is the student’s?","options":["It needs a lot of space.","It is expensive.","Both."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"People assume\" introduces the distractor; \"what really matters\" gives the student’s view.","tr":"\"People assume\" çeldiriciyi getiriyor; \"what really matters\" öğrencinin görüşünü veriyor.","fa":"«people assume» گزینه‌ی انحرافی را می‌آورد؛ «what really matters» نظر دانشجو را می‌دهد."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"You have used letters A, D and G in Questions 25-30. Can you use D again?","options":["Yes: letters can be repeated","Only for the last question","No: choose six answers, each letter once"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Choose SIX answers from the box\" means each letter is used once at most.","tr":"\"Kutudan ALTI cevap seç\", her harfin en fazla bir kez kullanılması demektir.","fa":"«شش جواب از کادر انتخاب کن» یعنی هر حرف حداکثر یک بار به کار می‌رود."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"For \"Which TWO things will they include?\", one student says \"That’s been done before\" about an idea. What does this usually mean?","options":["The idea is chosen","The idea is probably dropped","The other student must decide"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A reason against an idea usually means it is not chosen, unless the other student defends it.","tr":"Bir fikre karşı bir neden, öbür öğrenci savunmadıkça genelde seçilmediği anlamına gelir.","fa":"دلیلی علیه یک ایده معمولاً یعنی انتخاب نمی‌شود، مگر اینکه دانشجوی دیگر از آن دفاع کند."}}],"id":"c-x09-l3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-l3"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
